course: dictionary
lesson: 7155
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Perform is one of them. «Professional recorder players still perform today.» Look at the words around it: recorder players and music. So perform means to play music for an audience.
explain: Now read «In science, you perform an experiment.» Here there is no stage. You do the experiment, so perform means to carry out or do something carefully. Always ask: what does the sentence need the word to mean? Then swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Perform can also describe how well someone works. «Players perform well in a match» means they play well, and «perform badly» means they do not. The word tells you about the quality of the work. Look for words like well, badly, task or stage to find the right meaning.
explain: Perform is a verb that changes its ending: perform, performs, performed, performing. «The Greeks performed comedies» uses the past tense. Spotting the ending helps you read faster and understand more.
fact: «Perform» means to act, sing, dance or play music for an audience.
fact: «Perform» can also mean to do a task, especially a difficult or exact one, such as perform a calculation or an operation.
fact: «Perform» can mean to work or do well or badly, as in «players perform well in a match».
fact: «Performance nerves» means the fear of performing, and it often fades once you start.
fact: The verb changes its ending: perform, performs, performed, performing.
exercise: «Professional recorder players still perform today.» What does perform mean here? | To fall over | To hide | *To play music for an audience | To wash up
exercise: In science, you perform an experiment. What does perform mean here? | *To carry it out carefully | To eat it | To paint it | To forget it
exercise: «The Greeks performed comedies in open-air theatres.» Find and copy the word that is a form of perform. | open | Greeks | *performed | theatres
test: «The New Zealand rugby team performs a haka before matches.» What does performs mean here? | Goes home | *Does a traditional dance or action before the match | Stops running | Eats lunch
test: Maya says stage fright is the fear of performing. Which meaning is closest? | *Fear of acting, singing or playing for an audience | Wanting to sleep | Being happy in a play | Fear of the dark
exam: «When someone performs, you listen quietly and clap at the end.» Why do you clap? | Because the music is too loud | *To show respect for their effort | To wake them up | To say goodbye
